# sddra — Project Documentation

Purpose:
  Project documentation mapping for sddra.ai.
  Maps human-readable docs to their .sdd counterparts
  and defines audience, ownership, and freshness rules.

Documents:
  - ../README.md — Root human-readable entry point (UPDATED 2026-09-02)
  - ../AGENT_README.md — Agent-specific instructions
  - ../CLAUDE.md — Claude Code instructions
  - .claude/docs/README.md — Documentation system overview
  - .claude/docs/INDEX.md — Human docs master index
  - .sdd/docs/INDEX.md — Machine docs master index
  - .sdd/docs/overview/sdd-overview.md — System overview
  - .sdd/docs/commands/reference.md — Command reference
  - .sdd/docs/commands/workflow.md — Workflow guidance
  - .sdd/docs/commands/auto-chain.md — AUTO chain engine docs
  - .sdd/docs/analysis/system-analysis.md — Deep system analysis
  - .sdd/docs/analysis/heretic-analysis.md — External tool analysis
  - .sdd/docs/appendices/glossary.md — Terminology

Audience:
  HUMAN — Project users, contributors
  DEVELOPER — Implementation team
  AI — Autonomous agents working on the project

DocDepth:
  L0: What is this? (README.md)
  L1: What, Why, How (docs/)
  L2: Architecture, Dependencies (STRUCTURE.md, MAP.md)
  L3: Operations, Monitoring (runtime/, gates/)
  L4: Scaling, Security (evolution/, agent/)
  L5: Compliance, Audit (governance/, security-events.sdd)

State: +
